From: NetVOB_MiSTer feat-decoder-bringup
Subject: [PATCH] emu.sv: fix malformed S0 CONF_STR extension list ("MPG M2V" -> "MPGM2V")

The MiSTer config-string {Ext} field is a CONCATENATED list of 3-character
extensions with NO separators (official docs: "BINGEN" = BIN + GEN; example
"S0,CUECHD,Insert CD;"). The fork shipped "S0,MPG M2V,Load Video;" with a SPACE,
which is malformed: the 7-char field isn't a multiple of 3, so the Main binary
chunks it as {"MPG", " M2", "V.."} — a corrupt slot-0 extension filter.

Symptom this fixes (verified on hardware): a `.mgl` `<file type="s" index="0"
path="test.mpg">` mount of a CONFIRMED-present, valid 1.99 MB MPEG-2 ES never
registers img_mounted[0]/img_size — mpg_streamer reports total_sectors=0 (uart_debug
Z:0000 T:0), so the decoder gets no bitstream and the screen is black, even though
the decoder/mem_shim/analog all initialize correctly. File-not-found was ruled out
by staging the clip and re-confirming Z=0.

Fix: "S0,MPGM2V,Load Video;" — slot 0 accepts .MPG and .M2V (both valid 3-char
extensions for our elementary-stream test clips), correctly formatted.

--- a/rtl/emu.sv
+++ b/rtl/emu.sv
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@
 parameter CONF_STR = {
     "MPEG2;;",
-    "S0,MPG M2V,Load Video;",
+    "S0,MPGM2V,Load Video;",
     "O1,Aspect Ratio,4:3,16:9;",
     "O[10],Direct Video,Off,On;",
     "R0,Reset;",
